2. **Compose CLI compatibility (MANDATORY)**:
   - Support both `docker compose` (plugin) and `docker-compose` (standalone) via a runtime
     fallback: check `docker compose version` first; if that fails, try `command -v docker-compose`
     and fall back to `/usr/local/bin/docker-compose` if found.
   - Never hard-code the compose binary — always use the fallback wrapper.

3. **Layered, tool-agnostic health gates (MANDATORY)**:
   - Prefer compose status checks, host-side endpoint probes, and small app-level
     end-to-end checks over invasive exec probes.
   - Do not assume every local service registers itself with service discovery —
     always verify via compose or port-level probes.
   - do NOT make `docker compose exec ... mongo`, `mongosh`, `memcached-tool`, or
     similar dependency-local tools a required health gate — these may not exist inside
     the container and will cause false failures.
   - Bound every external probe with an explicit timeout guard: use `nc -w <seconds>` for
     netcat, `curl --max-time <seconds>` for HTTP, and `timeout <seconds>` for exec checks.
   - Every `docker compose exec` probe must pass `-T` (no-TTY) to stay non-interactive.

